      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T13:06:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure. I see the issue that could occur with timer-handle re-use, and rather went with a flag \u0027expiry_pending\u0027 in the `sfdp_session_timer_t` struct.\n\nThis flag is checked in timer-refresh paths to ensure any packets in-flight does not attempt to update the access/update the timer wheel of a sfdp session which has been marked for expiry.\n\nConcerning the test modification you propose, I don\u0027t think it is that easy to verify this scenario. Since a call to sfdp_kill_session_batch also results in a call to vlib_node_set_interrupt_pending() for the sfdp-expire node, it would be difficult to \u0027stack\u0027 batches of sfdp sessions to expire unless we add additional plumbing in SFDP code to stop the sfdp-expire node from being scheduled to run right after the batch \u0026 reproduce a \u0027stacking\u0027 scenario particularly for the test. Since this is a test API that it not expected to be used in production scenario, would it be fine if we omit such test for now ?",
